{
  "title": "Spread Across Every Stretch",
  "description": "## Task\n\nTake every non-empty stretch of consecutive values in a list. The spread of a stretch is its largest value minus its smallest value (a one-value stretch has spread 0). Add up the spreads of all stretches. Because the total can be huge, return it modulo 1,000,000,007.\n\n## Input\n\n- `values` — a list of integers. It may be empty.\n\n## Output\n\nAn integer: the sum of the spreads of all non-empty stretches, modulo 1000000007.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nspread_across_every_stretch([1, 3, 2])  # returns 5\nspread_across_every_stretch([5, 5, 5])  # returns 0\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 ≤ length of `values` ≤ 10^5\n- -10^9 ≤ each value ≤ 10^9\n- With 10^5 values there are about 5 billion stretches, so looking at each one is too slow.\n",
  "signature": "def spread_across_every_stretch(values: list[int]) -> int",
